{"name":"Nocturnal Expedition","hex":"#114c5a","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"nocturnal","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a person, creature, group, or species, primarily active during the night.","Of an occurrence, taking place at night, nightly."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A person or creature that is active at night.","A device for telling the time at night, rather like a sundial but read according to the stars."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/nocturnal"},{"term":"expedition","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A military journey; an enterprise against some enemy or into enemy territory.","An important or long journey, for example a march or a voyage."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To take part in a trip or expedition; to travel."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/expedition"}],"entries":[{"title":"Nocturnal animal","blocks":[{"text":"Nocturnality is a behavior in some non-human animals characterized by being active during the night and sleeping during the day. The common adjective is nocturnal, with diurnal meaning the opposite."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1d/Owl_at_Night.jpg/330px-Owl_at_Night.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nocturnal_animal","wikidata":"Q309179"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/de/Kiwi_bird_in_Christchurch%2C_New_Zealand%2C_2002-01-01.jpg/500px-Kiwi_bird_in_Christchurch%2C_New_Zealand%2C_2002-01-01.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/de/Kiwi_bird_in_Christchurch%2C_New_Zealand%2C_2002-01-01.jpg/1280px-Kiwi_bird_in_Christchurch%2C_New_Zealand%2C_2002-01-01.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d